; RFC 9943 (SCITT Architecture) — Section 7, "Transparent Statements"
; Figure 7: "CDDL Definition for a Transparent Statement"
; Source: rfc9943.txt lines 1141-1145; figure caption at line 1147.
; The RFC calls this a "normative CDDL definition of Transparent Statements".
;
; Copied VERBATIM, including the RFC's three-column left margin and the
; two spaces before "=>". Nothing added, removed, reordered, or realigned.
;
; COSE_Sign1 is deliberately NOT restated here. Section 7 says: "See Figure 3
; for the CDDL rule that defines COSE_Sign1 as specified in Section 4.2 of
; RFC 9052 [STD96]." -> see signed-statement-receipt.cddl.
;
; DEFECT, kept verbatim: this block REDEFINES the rule name
; Unprotected_Header, which Figure 3 already defines differently. The two
; files therefore cannot be concatenated into a single CDDL model without a
; duplicate-rule-name error. Note also that this definition is a CLOSED map:
; it drops both the optional x5chain entry AND the `* label => any` socket
; that Figure 3 has. See README.md.

   Transparent_Statement = #6.18(COSE_Sign1)

   Unprotected_Header = {
     &(receipts: 394)  => [+ bstr .cbor Receipt]
   }
